  "observations": [
    "Round02 is meaningful progress: the muddy embossed blocks in round01 have become larger, clearer beveled stone masses. The blue lower body is readable and the old nearly black bottom band remains gone.",
    "N/S repeated native and independent views show regular vertical blue/cyan ribs between darker front stone centers. Each internal port neighborhood is broad in tone, not a one-pixel missing-coverage seam. The collar-tone-context diagnostic retains the exact native crop and locates original expanded published port x320 and576. These ribs remain visible at phone32 and interrupt the sense of a continuous stone course.",
    "The cyan crown and collar highlights are still relatively broad uniform fields against subdued cobalt faces. There is better faceting than round01, but the highlight/midtone organization does not yet give the softly finished stone character demonstrated by the fixed target. The lower stone shoulders should retain their new clearer form while the full wall receives more coherent light/material integration.",
    "E/W have useful new crown division and rounded cap shading. No old round01 interior-groove location was treated as a current port failure. Current actual true-port samples are smooth; actual matching revised fields are permitted and do not need to revert to round01.",
    "No black holes, clipping, alpha puncture, cap erasure, overhang, directional ground shadow or local port geometry break was found in the bounded visual/native checks. The static blocking world-terrain role and finite strip are preserved.",
    "The current actual linked normal-dependent native radiance graph is valid within preconstruction method freedom. Its emission output or change from an older graph is not a blocker. The remaining issue concerns the visible color/highlight organization, and may be solved with any coherent native geometry/normal/material/light treatment satisfying the unchanged contract."
  ],
